      "She stepped out of the shed into full sunlight and looked down the hill. From here the orchard lay spread out below her, rank on rank of bare-fruited trees falling away toward the lake, and at the bottom of the slope, set against the dark line of the lower wall, stood a small white cottage with a slate roof and a green door and a single chimney, from which, even at this hour, a thin straight thread of smoke was rising into the windless air. In the cottage’s upper window something caught the light, a small bright flash, there and gone, like a coin turned over in a hand.",
